[36m(TaskRunner pid=286723)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=286723)[0m A divisor of \(9!\) that ends in 1 must be congruent to 1 modulo 10. Such divisors must be coprime to 10, meaning they cannot be divisible by 2 or 5. Therefore, we consider the divisors of \(3^4 \times 7\) (since we remove the factors of 2 and 5 from \(9!\)).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=286723)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=286723)[0m The sum of the divisors of \(3^4 \times 7\) is calculated as follows:
